'''Farsin Kappehl'''<ref name="UVG" /> was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Rebel trooper|soldier]] who served in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|early rebellion]] against the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Serving as a [[private]], Kappehl was one of several volunteers who joined an improvised squad of rebel fighters, codenamed "[[Rogue One]]," who took it upon themselves to [[Battle of Scarif|steal]] the [[Death Star plans|plans]] of the Imperial [[superweapon]] known as the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. While the mission was a success, Kappehl and the rest of his team lost their lives in the opening battle of the war.<ref name="Rogue One" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Farsin Kappehl was portrayed by [[Dan Euston]] in ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Facebook">{{Facebook|username=LondonFilmandComicCon|url=LondonFilmandComicCon/photos/877358262448719|name=London Film and Comic Con|date=2018-07-19|quote=We have more interesting Star Wars guests attending! DANIEL EUSTON will be appearing at London Film & Comic Con on Sunday 29th July at Olympia London. Daniel was one of the Elite Praetorian guards in Star Wars: The Last Jedi. Daniel also played a First Order and an Empire Stormtrooper, a Rebel Alliance Resistance Bombardier, and was the stunt double for Poe Dameron in both The Force Awakens and The Last Jedi. Daniel was also part of the Guavian Death Gang, a Rebel Alliance Pilot, and Private Farsin Kappehl in Jyn Erso's rebel marine squad|archivedate=20220518185541}}</ref>

